    faq: [
      { q: 'Is 2027 a good year for Jia Wood?', a: 'Good for output, mixed for patience. Ding Fire is the Hurting Officer for Jia — talent, expression, and a low tolerance for authority — landing on Wei Earth, which is Direct Wealth, real earnings. If you make things, sell things, or teach, the year rewards you. If your job is mostly obeying, it tests you. Neither is fate; it is a weather forecast.' },
      { q: 'What does a Hurting Officer year mean?', a: 'The Hurting Officer is the star of what you produce: ideas, words, skills, creative work — and for women it also rivals the partner star. In a Hurting Officer year you are more expressive and less obedient. Handled well, it means recognition and new income from your own talent; handled badly, arguments with bosses and impulsive exits.' },
      { q: 'When should Jia Wood make money moves in 2027?', a: 'Aim for the Wealth months: Jia Chen from 5 April (Indirect Wealth in the branch, your own Friend on the stem), Ji You from 8 September (Direct Wealth stem, Direct Officer branch), and Gui Chou from 6 January 2028. Avoid big commitments in the Ding Wei month from 7 July, when the year theme doubles and the talking outruns the counting.' }
    ]
